<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Litold of Znojmo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1112</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Litold was a Přemyslid prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, son of Conrad I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a>. He received the Znojmo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> around 1092, when his father became Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. He ruled Znojmo until his death in 1112, taking part in the dynasty's quarrels over the Bohemian throne, and his descendants continued to rule the Znojmo appanage.</p></div>
